WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:14.500
The Light List, published by the Coast Guard, describes every aid in its region: name and position, light characteristic, height above water, nominal range, the structure, and remarks such as sector bearings or fog signals.

2
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.400
It’s divided into seven volumes.

3
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:29.200
Volume three covers the Atlantic and Gulf coasts from Little River, South Carolina, around Florida to the Econfina River in the Big Bend, so it includes most of Florida.

4
00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.125
Volume four continues along the Gulf to Texas.

5
00:00:33.375 --> 00:00:38.300
Check the Local Notice to Mariners for changes since the edition you’re using.
